From ae226a26443a5114f03b8e3f0d318765311f7b50 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 06:25:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Block 11A: inspection performance + live camera lifecycle

- apps/reality_painter/app.py: vision/mirror stages are now ungated -
  the camera stays live in every RuntimeMode, not just PAINTING_MODES.
  Only the interaction/painting pipeline (tracking, gesture, cursor,
  action, mouse control, painting, overlay) remains gated off during
  INSPECTING_3D.
- apps/reality_painter/mode_router.py: removed the now-obsolete
  _freeze_frame() mechanism - it existed only because vision used to
  be gated off during INSPECTING_3D. Entering 3D now only flips the
  mode; context['frame'] is left alone.
- apps/reality_painter/asset_render.py: create_asset_render_stage now
  caches the expensive Renderer3D.render() call, keyed by each scene
  object's (name, transform). The cache is only invalidated when a
  transform actually changes (e.g. via the existing A/D/W/S/+/-/R
  inspection controls) - a fresh camera frame every cycle no longer
  forces a re-render, and no longer accumulates composited output
  onto a stale frozen frame.
- tests/test_runtime_mode.py: updated the two assertions that tested
  the old freeze-frame behavior to assert the new, intended live-
  camera contract instead (same test file, same scope).
- tests/test_block11a_inspection_perf.py (new): focused cache-
  invalidation + live-camera regression tests.
